# Sibling-type resolution inside Common/ relies on this explicit index; a
# directory carrying a qmldir is no longer implicitly scanned, so every
# Common/*.qml type must be listed. qmldir.test.cjs enforces that.
#
# T3Socket.qml is deliberately absent, and must stay absent. It is the
# only file here that imports QtWebSockets, which is an optional package
# (qt6-qtwebsockets-devel). T3Code.qml pulls it in through a Loader by
# URL instead, so a machine without the package gets Loader.Error on that
# one object — a T3 chip that says why it is off — rather than a failure
# to resolve a registered type. qmldir.test.cjs carries the exemption.

singleton Theme Theme.qml
singleton Popouts Popouts.qml
singleton Screens Screens.qml
singleton Launcher Launcher.qml
singleton Usage Usage.qml
singleton T3Code T3Code.qml
singleton T3Connection T3Connection.qml
singleton T3Rpc T3Rpc.qml
singleton T3Threads T3Threads.qml
singleton Notifs Notifs.qml
singleton SysInfo SysInfo.qml
singleton Osd Osd.qml
singleton Weather Weather.qml
singleton Wallpaper Wallpaper.qml
singleton Settings Settings.qml
singleton Audio Audio.qml
singleton WifiState WifiState.qml
singleton BluetoothState BluetoothState.qml
singleton Battery Battery.qml
singleton Media Media.qml
singleton Tailscale Tailscale.qml

# Plain types (not singletons)
Claim Claim.qml
